+````markdown name=Aegis_one_pager.md
+# Aegis — Trusted MLOps & Model Governance Platform
+
+Elevator pitch
+- Aegis is an auditable MLOps and governance control plane that makes every model — from training to edge — provable, verifiable and safe to operate. We combine cryptographic signing, immutable transparency logs, human‑in‑the‑loop approvals, and a canonical Model Context Protocol (MCP) to give operators, safety teams and auditors a single source of truth for model provenance and decisions.
+
+Who it’s for
+- Regulated enterprises and mission‑critical systems: healthcare providers (HIPAA/HITRUST), automotive & mobility (safety cases), aerospace/defense (supply‑chain integrity), financial services (auditable pricing models), and any org that needs non‑repudiable model lineage.
+
+Key value props
+- Provable provenance: every promoted model is signed (Vault Transit & cosign) and logged immutably to Rekor — evidence bundles (MLflow + attestations) are attached and indexed in MCP.
+- Human safety & compliance: require HIL approvals with non‑repudiable signed receipts recorded in Rekor; integrate approvals into CI pipelines with automated pausing/resumption workflows.
+- Safe edge & OTA: device agents only load signed artifacts (cosign + Rekor + TPM/TEE), support dual‑partition updates, staged canaries, and validated rollback drills.
+- Federated & privacy‑preserving learning: secure aggregation + DP harnesses for cross‑site improvements without centralizing raw data — with poisoning tests and privacy reporting.
+- Audit & incident readiness: compile audit packets (evidence bundle + Vault audit logs + HIL receipts) for regulators or internal auditors; fast incident forensics via n8n automation and MCP queries.
+
+Core components (at a glance)
+- MCP (Model Context Protocol): single API to upsert/search model context (artifact, datasets, attestations, HIL approvals, deployments).
+- Signing & transparency: Vault (BYOK/HSM) for signing, cosign integration, Rekor transparency logs for immutable proofs.
+- Automation & HIL: n8n workflows for approvals, remediation and incident orchestration; receipt_signer for signed HIL receipts.
+- Enforcement: Gatekeeper + pre‑load webhook enforce only‑approved models in Kubernetes/edge deployments.
+- Edge & OTA: hardened pre‑load verifier, dual‑partition updates, TUF/TUF‑style manifests and rollback runbooks.
+- Federated + DP: Flower/TFF integration, poisoning test harness, DP post‑aggregation tools and reporting.
+
+Deployment models
+- Managed Aegis (SaaS): fastest path to POC (BYOK option for signing keys).
+- Dedicated tenant: single‑tenant in customer VPC with HSM/BYOK (recommended for regulated production).
+- On‑prem appliance: for fully air‑gapped or classified environments.
+
+Security & compliance
+- BYOK/HSM key custody, Vault audit logging, Rekor immutable logs, SCA in CI and pentest scaffolding. Evidence bundles map to HIPAA/HITRUST/ISO/UL checklists for audits.
+
+Pilot offer (8–12 weeks)
+- Deliverables: CI→sign→Rekor POC, MCP integration for one model, n8n HIL workflow, Gatekeeper enforcement dry‑run, edge HIL rig verification and a compliance packet for auditors.
+- KPI highlights: attestation coverage ≥ 95%, HIL traceability 100%, OTA rollback drill < 15 minutes on testbed.
+
+Why Aegis vs alternatives
+- Combines the best open standards (Sigstore, SLSA) and enterprise-grade KMS/HSM patterns into a single control plane (MCP) with built‑in HIL, federated privacy tooling and edge safety patterns — a complete, auditable model supply‑chain.
+
+Next steps
+- Request a pilot SOW targeted to your use case (clinical, autonomy, launch ops) — we'll provide the SOW, runbooks and an environment checklist for a rapid POC.
+
+Contact
+- aegis@yourorg.example | https://aegis.example.com
+````
