+````markdown name=Evidence_Bundle_Spec.md
+# Aegis Evidence Bundle Specification — v1.0
+
+Purpose
+- The Evidence Bundle is the canonical JSON payload that collects provenance artifacts produced during model build/promotion. It is designed to be attachable to MLflow runs, uploaded to object storage (S3/GCS), indexed by the MCP, and linked to Rekor/cosign attestations for audit and forensic use.
+
+Compatibility & Goals
+- Compatible with Sigstore/cosign + Rekor workflows and MLflow model artifacts.
+- Designed for regulatory evidence, reproducibility and incident forensics.
+- Minimal PII surface: do not include raw PHI; include dataset references (IDs/URIs) and retention/deletion metadata to allow DSAR processing.
+
+Versioning
+- schema_version: major.minor (e.g., "1.0"). Incompatible schema changes increment major.
+
+Top-level JSON schema (concise)
+```json
+{
+  "schema_version": "1.0",
+  "model_id": "string",
+  "version": "string",
+  "artifact": {
+    "uri": "s3://bucket/path/model.tar.gz",
+    "digest": "sha256:...",
+    "size": 12345678
+  },
+  "mlflow": {
+    "run_id": "string",
+    "tracking_uri": "https://mlflow.example.com"
+  },
+  "build": {
+    "ci_run_id": "string",
+    "commit": "gitsha",
+    "builder": "docker://image:tag",
+    "build_logs_uri": "s3://..."
+  },
+  "datasets": [
+    {
+      "dataset_id": "dset-123",
+      "version": "v2",
+      "location": "s3://datasets/dset-123/v2/",
+      "deid_status": "deidentified|pseudonymized|raw_restricted",
+      "notes": "clinical informatics validation id: 42"
+    }
+  ],
+  "training": {
+    "hyperparameters": { "lr": 0.001 },
+    "train_command": "python train.py --config",
+    "environment": { "python": "3.11", "pytorch": "2.2" }
+  },
+  "evaluation": {
+    "datasets": ["dset-123/test"],
+    "metrics": { "auc": 0.92, "precision": 0.85 },
+    "evaluation_artifact_uri": "s3://..."
+  },
+  "attestations": [
+    {
+      "type": "vault-transit|cosign",
+      "rekor_index": 12345,
+      "attestation_uri": "https://rekor.example.com/entry/12345",
+      "signed_at": "2026-02-14T12:00:00Z"
+    }
+  ],
+  "hil_approvals": [
+    {
+      "approver_id": "alice@example.com",
+      "role": "SafetyEngineer",
+      "receipt_rekor_index": 23456,
+      "signed_at": "2026-02-14T13:00:00Z",
+      "notes": "Checked checklist X, simulation run Y passed"
+    }
+  ],
+  "deployments": [
+    {
+      "env": "staging",
+      "cluster": "k8s-staging",
+      "namespace": "models",
+      "deployment_id": "deploy-abc",
+      "status": "promoted",
+      "deployed_at": "2026-02-14T14:00:00Z"
+    }
+  ],
+  "federated_rounds": [
+    { "round_id": "fr-2026-02-10-1", "rekor_index": 34567, "ts": "2026-02-10T09:00:00Z" }
+  ],
+  "compliance": {
+    "hipaa": { "contains_phi": false, "dsar_handle_id": null },
+    "export_control": { "itar": false }
+  },
+  "retention": {
+    "evidence_retention_days": 3650,
+    "data_retention_policy_id": "policy-7"
+  },
+  "notes": "Freeform operator notes and references"
+}
+```
+
+Field guidance & best practices
+- schema_version: always include and the MCP must record it.
+- model_id/version: canonical identifiers used by MCP (human readable and unique within tenant).
+- artifact.uri & digest: artifact must be content‑addressable (digest) — prefer sha256:hex.
+- mlflow.run_id: link back to training experiment; do not embed raw datasets or PHI.
+- datasets: reference by dataset_id and canonical storage URI. Include deid_status to help compliance teams.
+- attestations: include Rekor indices and attestation URI so auditors can fetch the evidence and transparency proofs.
+- hil_approvals: include approver identity (SSO email or subject), role and receipt Rekor index (signed receipt). Add checklist references.
+- deployments: list known deployments (environments) and statuses; for edge devices include device_id and OTA manifest ref when available.
+- federated_rounds: link to federated coordinator round IDs and Rekor logging for rounds.
+- compliance: flags for PHI and export control for rapid triage.
+- retention: encode evidence retention policy and DSAR handling pointers.
+
+Security & PII rules
+- Never place raw PHI inside the evidence bundle JSON when it will leave hospital or controlled environments. Use dataset references and de‑identification metadata.
+- If PII/PHI must be recorded for an internal audit, ensure the evidence bundle is stored encrypted and access controlled (Vault + object storage ACLs).
+- Sanitize user‑entered freeform notes to avoid leaking PHI.
+
+How evidence bundles are used
+- CI: build job generates evidence bundle after signing and uploads to artifact store; then upserts MCP with bundle URL.
+- MCP: stores the evidence bundle pointer and indexes fields for search and audit; subscribers (Gatekeeper, n8n) can fetch bundle for enforcement or display.
+- Rekor: attestations are published and rekor_index referenced in the bundle.
+- Auditors: request evidence bundle export for model versions and time windows; MCP provides the index.
+
+Publishing & discovery
+- Evidence bundles are uploaded to an S3/GCS bucket under a tenant path: `s3://aegis-evidence/{tenant}/{model_id}/{version}/evidence_v1.json`
+- MCP stores the canonical pointer (evidence_uri) and records in DB; Rekor links remain the ground truth for signatures.
+
+Example minimal bundle (realistic)
+```json
+{
+  "schema_version":"1.0",
+  "model_id":"ed-triage",
+  "version":"v1.2.0",
+  "artifact": { "uri":"s3://aegis-artifacts/ed-triage/v1.2.0/model.tar.gz", "digest":"sha256:abcd..." },
+  "mlflow":{"run_id":"run-0a1b2c","tracking_uri":"https://mlflow.internal"},
+  "build":{"ci_run_id":"gha-123","commit":"abc123"},
+  "attestations":[{"type":"cosign","rekor_index":98765,"attestation_uri":"https://rekor.internal/entry/98765","signed_at":"2026-02-14T12:00:00Z"}],
+  "hil_approvals":[{"approver_id":"dr.jane@ech.org","role":"PhysicianReviewer","receipt_rekor_index":98766,"signed_at":"2026-02-14T13:00:00Z","notes":"Clinical validation OK"}],
+  "compliance":{"hipaa":{"contains_phi":false}}
+}
+```
+
+Versioning & evolution
+- Include `schema_version` in every bundle. MCP must store the schema version.
+- Additive changes: introduce new fields and bump minor (e.g., 1.1 → 1.2). Consumers must ignore unknown fields if they are forward compatible.
+- Breaking changes: bump major (1.x → 2.0) and publish migration guidance; keep old schema supported for a deprecation window (e.g., 6 months).
+
+APIs that consume bundles (recommended)
+- MCP: ingest and index bundle metadata; expose evidence_uri and Rekor indices via API.
+- Gatekeeper pre‑load webhook: fetch evidence bundle and validate HIL approvals and attestations before allowing load.
+- n8n: fetch bundle to populate approval UIs and incident packets.
+- Auditor export API: allow time‑bounded evidence export in a tamper‑evident zip (bundle + Rekor proofs + Vault audit excerpts).
+
+Operational checklist (before a pilot handles sensitive data)
+1. Confirm BAA and legal approvals if PHI is involved.  
+2. Ensure evidence buckets are encrypted with tenant KMS (BYOK) and access is restricted.  
+3. Ensure MCP and Rekor endpoints are inside the approved network perimeter (air‑gapped if required).  
+4. Validate retention policy and DSAR runbooks for bundle deletion/exports.
+
+Publishing the Spec
+- Host this spec in your public or partner docs repo with versioning (e.g., /specs/evidence-bundle/v1.0.md).
+- Provide reference code to generate/upload bundles (CI snippets already included in Aegis).
+- Encourage partner integrations (MLflow, registries, OTA servers) to adopt the bundle schema and post to MCP.
+
